 "synopsis": "Indira IVF, backed by EQT Partners, is in discussions to acquire a 70-75% stake in Sabine Hospital and Research Centre in a transaction proposed to value Sabine at ₹1,200-1,300 crore. The deal involves purchasing a stake from current owner CX Partners and additional stake from founder Dr Sabine Sivadasan. Sabine operates two facilities in Kerala providing fertility and maternal healthcare services. Investment bank O3 Capital is advising CX Partners on the exit plan. Indira IVF is concurrently preparing for a ₹3,500-crore initial public offering.",
